{
  "_comment": [
    "catalogue.json — the ONE definition of the app's roles and their modules.",
    "",
    "Four consumers read this file and nothing else:",
    "  index.php               resolves /apps/{role}/{module} to a role + module",
    "  js/modules/registry.js  (via window.APP_CATALOGUE, injected by index.php)",
    "  api/config/modules.php  server-side allowlist for the workspace endpoints",
    "  tools/_unused/harness.js reads it straight off disk",
    "There is deliberately no second copy of this list anywhere.",
    "",
    "The twelve programs and their order match the marketing site's",
    "'For Enterprises' and 'For Leaders' module lists. Keep them in step: the",
    "site is where people meet these names first.",
    "",
    "role.key   stable identifier — used in the database (organizations.account_type)",
    "role.slug  the URL segment: /apps/{slug}/...",
    "",
    "module.id     STORAGE key. It is the workspaces.module column, the",
    "              localStorage namespace and the coach/help scope. Once a",
    "              module has data, NEVER change it. 'pipeline' and",
    "              'exec-readiness' predate everything here and are frozen.",
    "module.slug   URL segment: /apps/{role.slug}/{module.slug}. Safe to rename —",
    "              list the old one in $LEGACY_MODULE_SLUGS in index.php and it",
    "              301s to the new address instead of going dead.",
    "module.tag    the discipline line under the name on the site and the",
    "              launchpad — short, uppercase, no sentence.",
    "module.status 'live' = has its own code | 'planned' = renders the shared",
    "              placeholder. Flip to 'live' when you point scripts at real code.",
    "module.scripts/styles/templates/tabs/logo/title — see js/modules/registry.js.",
    "",
    "To add a module: append an entry, create js/modules/<id>/module.js calling",
    "Modules.define(), set status to 'live'. Nothing else needs editing — the",
    "server allowlist, the router, the launchpad and the switcher all read here."
  ],
